  "shared_masks_across_groups": {
    "has_history_mask": "gates 6 USER_HISTORY features (log1p_prev_view_count, log1p_prev_session_count, recent_history_length, has_history, recent_distinct_items, recent_distinct_known_main_categories); must survive removal of every other USER_HISTORY column.",
    "recent_category_match_supported": "gates recent_category_match_share only; shared between USER_HISTORY and CATEGORY closures.",
    "recent_brand_match_supported": "gates recent_brand_match_share only; shared between USER_HISTORY and BRAND closures.",
    "recent_price_supported": "gates recent_mean_log_price AND current_minus_recent_mean_log_price; shared between USER_HISTORY and PRICE closures.",
    "prev_user_event_available": "gates log1p_time_since_prev_user_event_s; shared between USER_HISTORY and ELAPSED_TIME closures.",
    "prev_session_available": "gates log1p_time_since_prev_session_last_event_s; shared between USER_HISTORY and ELAPSED_TIME closures.",
    "price_missing / price_zero / price_conflict": "gate log1p_price; price_zero is a proven (data-measured) exact duplicate of price_missing in this dataset (PROTOCOL_DEVIATIONS.md:69-76), so removing price_missing without removing price_zero would silently keep the same information.",
    "prev_gap_unavailable": "gates log1p_prev_raw_view_gap_s only; ELAPSED_TIME-local.",
    "item_age_unavailable": "gates log1p_item_observed_age_s; shared between PRODUCT and ELAPSED_TIME-flavoured closures."
  },
  "notes": [
    "direct_owner assigns each feature to exactly ONE semantic group per the task packet's enum; features that are formally computed from another group's tokens (e.g. daypart/weekday from block_ts, prefix_known_category_count from main_category_tokens) are still counted under their own thematic group (CALENDAR / SESSION_INTENT) but list the true upstream dependency in dependency_edges.",
    "total_closure additions beyond the formal dependency graph are DOCUMENTED duplications already proven or derived in REDUNDANCY_FINDINGS.md (e.g. is_weekend/daypart/weekday all disclose the same local-time signal as local_hour_sin/cos+local_weekday_sin/cos); they are listed so a group's total information content is not undercounted just because no single column literally reads another as an input.",
    "source_refs for every edge are in audit/FEATURE_INVENTORY.csv (depends_on / duplicates_or_derivations columns) and audit/TRANSFORM_LINEAGE.json; this file is the graph view, not a new source of claims."
  ]
}